### 4. Configurable Media Storage & Delivery Abstraction Layer
- **Action**: Implement `src/lib/media/resolver.ts` using the Provider Strategy Pattern.
- **Resolver Logic**:
  ```typescript
  export interface MediaTransformOptions {
    width?: number;
    height?: number;
    quality?: 'auto' | number;
    format?: 'auto' | 'webp' | 'avif' | 'mp4' | 'webm';
    video?: boolean;
  }

  export function resolveMediaUrl(
    pathOrId: string,
    options: MediaTransformOptions = {},
    overrideConfig?: NGOConfig
  ): string
  ```
  - If `pathOrId` begins with `http://` or `https://` -> returns verbatim.
  - **Cloudinary Strategy**: If `provider === 'cloudinary'`, constructs dynamic transformation URL:
    `https://res.cloudinary.com/${cloudName}/${resourceType}/upload/${transforms}/${fullPath}`
    If Cloudinary is configured as provider but `cloudName` is unset or credentials are empty in local dev, cleanly falls back to `/media/${cleanPath}` so local visual assets render flawlessly.
  - **S3 / Cloudflare R2 / MinIO Strategy**: Constructs `${publicUrlBase}/${cleanPath}` or `https://${bucket}.s3.${region}.amazonaws.com/${cleanPath}`.
  - **Local / Docker Volume Strategy**: Resolves to `${basePath}/${cleanPath}` (e.g. `/media/...`).
- **Data-Saver & Performance Hook (`src/lib/media/use-media-optimization.ts`)**:
  - Detects `navigator.connection?.saveData` and connection type (`effectiveType === '2g' | '3g'`).
  - Automatically disables background auto-playing video streams on slow networks or data-saver mode, rendering the optimized WebP/SVG poster still with an explicit "Play Stream" manual control.
- **Next.js Remote Patterns (`next.config.ts`)**:
  - Configures `res.cloudinary.com`, `**.amazonaws.com`, and `**.r2.cloudflarestorage.com`.

